  "prefLabel": "Bcr 207.13 Ex parte Communications",
  "priorExpiration": "2012-07-16",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Bcr 207.13 Ex parte Communications. Once an adjudicative proceeding has been commenced, no party shall communicate with any participating board member or the presiding officer concerning the merits of the case except upon notice to all parties and in accordance with the rules of this chapter. Nor shall any party cause another person to make such communications or otherwise engage in conduct prohibited by RSA 541-A:36.\n\nSource. #8044, eff 2-17-04; ss by #10073, INTERIM, eff 1-17-12, EXPIRES: 7-16-12; ss by #10161, eff 7-13-12",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/bcr200.html"
